WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.140
So you might remember the birther movement,
which claimed that Barack Obama was not actually

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.750
eligible to be president because of some combination
of he was born in Kenya or he was Indonesian

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.880
or his dad was an American.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.620
Or he once a dog meat in Indonesia.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.620
Know?

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.310
Well, whatever the explanation was, it was
a ridiculous idea.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:24.869
Barack Obama was born in Hawaii, but it was
a hugely racially tinged movement, which actually

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:27.850
Donald Trump was at the front and center of.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.699
Trump was one of the loudest and most prominent
birthers for a period of months, if not more

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:37.050
than a year, talking about Barack Obama's
birth certificate and the entire thing.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:43.879
Now, within mere hours of Kamala Harris becoming
Joe Biden's running mate, the birthers are

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:45.319
instantly back.

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:50.739
It's almost like if you're not white, they
question whether you're really an American.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:53.179
That seems to be the underlying theme here.

00:00:53.179 --> 00:00:55.120
Suddenly, suddenly being put forward.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.069
Now, I on the one hand, I don't want to give
this too much oxygen, but I do want to lay

00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:01.499
it out generally for you.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:07.939
A guy named John Eastman tweeted, quote, Is
Kamala Harris eligible for the office of vice

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:09.090
president?

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.460
Here is my article published by Newsweek exploring
the issues.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.899
Short answer, it depends.

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:20.479
Now, why Newsweek even published this at all
is a good question.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:26.640
Eastman teaches law at Chapman University
and is a fellow at the Claremont Institute.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.469
If you research the Claremont Institute, you'll
find that there are right wing think tank

00:01:30.469 --> 00:01:36.030
that was supported very early of Donald Trump
and has stuck to Trump and Trump ism.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.929
Like, I don't know, super glue, whatever metaphor
you want to use.

00:01:39.929 --> 00:01:41.369
Um, no, of course.

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:44.219
Kamala Harris was born in Oakland, California.

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:49.140
What possible argument would there be that
she's not eligible to be the president or

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.140
vice president?

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:55.360
Now, remember, in order to be vice president,
you have to be constitutionally eligible to

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.400
be president.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.359
So that's why it's relevant.

00:01:58.359 --> 00:02:02.220
The argument is, I hope you're ready for this.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.320
Harris's dad is Jamaican and was not an American
citizen when Kamala Harris was born in I believe

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.360
it's 1964.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:17.770
Kamala Harris, his mom is from India and she
was not a U.S. citizen at the time that Kamala

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.820
Harris was born in Oakland, California.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:27.500
Thus, Kamala is not a natural born citizen
and thus could not be vice president because

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.520
she is ineligible to be president of the United
States.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:36.590
Now, in the article, Eastman goes really into
the weeds with arguments about the 14th Amendment

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.590
and the definition.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.020
Again, I mean, it's like Barack Obama.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.600
Number two, the arguments about what does
it mean to be natural born?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.140
It's Obama birther ism redux.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:53.850
And and by the way, they are only pushing
it further by saying this isn't only the law

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.420
today.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:02.340
It's about what the founders meant when they
established how citizenship is conferred.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.120
And we can't just look at court decisions
today, although they have some court decisions

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.350
they claim suggests Khamal is not eligible.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:16.320
It's also about interpreting the desires of
what the founders meant hundreds of years

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.320
ago.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.700
Now, there is a lot more to this.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:26.170
There is actually a real law conversation
that could be had, but in practice, it's only

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:30.220
being applied to Barack Obama and now to Kamala
Harris.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:34.681
In practice, this is the same racist birther
ism that we saw with Barack Obama.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.760
And my instinct is and I hope that this is
the case.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.020
I don't think it's going to get a lot of pickup.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.020
And part of the reason why isn't going to
be because it's completely baseless factually,

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.690
which it is completely baseless factually.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.690
With Obama.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.870
It was about the president, with Kamala Harris.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.930
It's about the V.P..

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.160
And I think that may keep it from getting
the attention it otherwise might.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.890
And, of course, you know, no one said this
about John McCain born in Panama.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:00.890
They're just fine accepting.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.890
Well, it was a military base and thus it's
fine.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:08.090
Nobody said this about Ted Cruz when he was
a candidate for the Republican nomination

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.670
in 2016, even though he was born in Canada.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:15.440
As you may or may not know, current British
Prime Minister Boris Johnson was an American

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.100
citizen because he was born, I believe it
was in Manhattan, although he has since renounced

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.100
it.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.100
That's no problem.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.810
But is Kamala Harris, born in Oakland, eligible
to be vice president?

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.630
All of a sudden now they have questions.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:34.410
It's the same dog whistle stuff and it's almost
it's too predictable.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:39.010
It's too on the nose that this is the direction
immediately.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:44.750
You have some pro Trump think tank legal scholar
talking about let's sort of hope that this

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:45.750
is it.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:45.852
But I did want to let you know that it was
going on.

